                <pb facs="0269" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9437: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-17T11:00:00+08:00">August 17, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 17—1 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Japanese making complete evacuation of Canton today. Japanese gunboat and
                    merchant vessel left this morning with most remaining residents and Consul
                    General and staff leave tonight. With his departure I become Senior Consul. I
                    have called meeting of foreign representatives for consultation and have
                    circularized Americans discussing situation and advising them to come to Shameen
                    at first sign of danger to facilitate evacuation if same becomes necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Linnell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
